<section class="pw-card pw-stack"><h2>Six Production Stages</h2><div class="pw-table-wrap"><table class="pw-table"><thead><tr><th>Stage / Owner</th><th>What to Do</th><th>What Happens Next</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><strong>1. RM & PM Issue</strong><p class="pw-muted">Store Manager</p></td><td>Review recipe quantities and warehouse stock. Save a full, partial or additional material request. Start the physical handover, then complete it after checking the materials and FIFO lots.</td><td>Issue posts once in the RM/PM ledger. The mixing operator receives the job.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>2. PCM Making</strong><p class="pw-muted">Mixing Operator</p></td><td>Start Mixing with the people count. Complete it with mixing method, chemical/water quantities, prepared PCM, unit and machine-fill time. Record any loss.</td><td>One complete PCM batch feeds production continuously. Pauses do not create additional pours or new mixes.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>3. Filling & Sealing</strong><p class="pw-muted">Production Operator / Manager</p></td><td>Use the separate Filling and Sealing screens in order. Record manual/automatic machine, output, power and any idle/breakdown/wastage details. The manager reviews the count derived from sealing and approves it.</td><td>Approved output enters the inspection queue.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>4. Quality Check</strong><p class="pw-muted">QC Inspector / Approver</p></td><td>Start Inspection. Record leak, pressure and physical results; account for all units as accepted, rejected or rework. Measure PCM recovered from failed units. An authorized approver confirms the decision.</td><td>Accepted output goes to Bundle. Rework returns to PCM handling on this same work order. Rejected units do not enter saleable FG.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>5. Bundle</strong><p class="pw-muted">Production / Packing Worker</p></td><td>Count physical bundles, units per bundle and loose accepted units. Review actual material usage and scrap; explain changes. Bundle units must equal QC accepted units.</td><td>Consumption is reconciled and one FG batch posts. Unused, unmixed materials may return; mixed PCM never returns as warehouse RM stock.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>6. FG Store</strong><p class="pw-muted">FG Receiver / Store Worker</p></td><td>Receive the released batch, start putaway, choose an approved bin inside the mapped FG warehouse and complete putaway.</td><td>The work order closes. Eligible FG can be allocated to its sales order and handed to packaging/dispatch.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="pw-card pw-stack"><h2>QC Recovery Loop</h2><p><strong>QC rework → PCM Making → Filling → Sealing → QC → Bundle.</strong></p><p>Previously accepted units remain linked to this order. Prepare only the recovered PCM available on the order; do not create another full initial mix or warehouse PCM item. Issue replacement packaging or extra material separately with a reason. The next filling run records how much recovered PCM was actually reused.</p><p>Final FG combines accepted quantities across QC rounds once. Reprocessing does not consume the original chemical recipe again; actual additional packaging, loss and unused materials remain in the material trace.</p></section>
<section class="pw-card pw-stack"><h2>Using Work Queues and History</h2><p><strong>Pending</strong> shows work waiting to start or approve. <strong>In Progress</strong> shows started operations. <strong>History</strong> shows saved records on its own page. Refreshing a page preserves a started run.</p><p>Start and Complete capture server times automatically. Validation errors stay on the job page so the worker can correct quantities. An authorized manager can correct completed timestamps only with an audit reason from View Order Trace.</p><p>Each worker sees and operates the steps assigned to their role and site. Recording and approving are separate permissions. Store Manager currently has all Stage test permissions; future worker roles can be restricted independently.</p></section>
<details class="pw-card"><summary>Terminology</summary><div class="pw-table-wrap mt-3"><table class="pw-table"><tbody>@foreach(['WO'=>'Work Order: one executable production job.','FG'=>'Finished Goods: accepted product ready for storage and later dispatch.','RM'=>'Raw Materials: chemicals, water and other inputs.','PM'=>'Packaging Materials: pouches, film and other production packaging.','PCM'=>'Phase Change Material: the prepared thermal-storage solution.','BOM'=>'Bill of Materials: material quantities required per finished-good unit.','SKU'=>'Stock Keeping Unit: the exact inventory item code.','UOM'=>'Unit of Measure, such as KG, L or EA.','QC'=>'Quality Check: leak, pressure and physical inspection.','FIFO'=>'First In, First Out: issue eligible older material lots first.','ATP'=>'Available to Promise: eligible FG stock available for customer-order allocation.','Rework'=>'Reprocess failed units on the same work order using recovered solution where applicable.','Bin'=>'An approved physical storage position inside the FG warehouse.','OEE'=>'Overall Equipment Effectiveness: machine availability, performance and quality.'] as $word=>$meaning)<tr><th>{{ $word }}</th><td>{{ $meaning }}</td></tr>@endforeach</tbody></table></div></details>
